r/10165-flimflamberge","name":"Flimflamberge","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10165_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"14"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-10T22:47:19-08:00","id":783943,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flimflamberge</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/783742-c20-anniversary-kiths-list?p=783881#post783881\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I really want the Adhene. Denizens of the Dreaming is my favourite book of the line, and I love every one of them.<br /> <br /> Plus they add that &quot;dark&quot; edge some people claim is missing from Changeling without being definitively evil or anything. They also help to shift away a bit from the Celtic-centric kithain while filling in a major gap in the Tuatha/Fomorian lore.</div> </div> </div> </div>Adhene, yes. Matt confirmed they'd be included with the Gallain over on RPGnet.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-10T23:05:48-08:00","id":783950,"title":"","content":"Nice! Thanks for letting me know!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":